To accompany my recent hint that it would be nice
if the drawbridge were disambiguated from the wall
for the purpose of tile displays, I suppose this
would be as good a time as any to suggest that
there be enough flavors of "@" to cater for all
possible roles, races, genders, [Maybe even
alignments/orientations? Dibs on the butch elf
template if so.], all smushed back into "@" for
ASCII play, so that tiles didn't have to be either
androgynous or ridiculous.

Playing a bare and barrel chested _female_
barbarian is a bit offputting, as is a female mage
with a long white beard, or a male Kop lieutenant
in halter and shorts, for a couple of the more
egregious examples in the tile set I patched up a
while ago.

This YAN(?)I could well extend to NPC's that are
capable of meaningful sexual dimorphism (rumor has
it that even dwarves can barely tell the
difference, so they might be safely skipped), or
differentiation between roles or alignments.
Races are already more or less there.

This has the advantage that artists get more
freedom of expression, the disadvantage that tile
files would at least double in size, and the big
tile size one's data volumes are an issue already.

Also it's a pretty worthless idea if none of the
artists would care.

Comments?

